{"term":"male","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ca4bc73869b88e014b","definition":"Belonging to the sex which typically produces sperm, or to the gender which is typically associated with it.","example":"male writers","pos":"adj","synonyms":["manly","mannish","masculine","pin"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, usually","register":"not-comparable, usually","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a16ab9321638c045c","definition":"Characteristic of this sex/gender. (Compare masculine, manly.)","example":"stereotypically male interests","pos":"adj","synonyms":["manly","mannish","masculine","pin"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, usually","register":"not-comparable, usually","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:802c8d8d2a79edcc1a","definition":"Tending to lead to or regulate the development of sexual characteristics typical of this sex.","example":"the male chromosome","pos":"adj","synonyms":["manly","mannish","masculine","pin"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, usually","register":"not-comparable, usually","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b66a542af29040cc71","definition":"Masculine; of the masculine grammatical gender.","example":"The teacher's voice inflects the pulse of nêhiyawêwin as he teaches us. He says a prayer in the first class. Nouns, we learn, have a gender. In French, nouns are male or female, but in Cree, nouns are living or non-living, animate or inanimate.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["manly","mannish","masculine","pin"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"form-of, masculine, not-comparable, usually","register":"form-of, masculine, not-comparable, usually","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8f01d895062df79b96","definition":"Having the F factor; able to impart DNA into another bacterium which does not have the F factor (a female).","example":"Furthermore, male bacteria with fi + R factors, which inhibit the function of F (fi fertility inhibition) (Watanabe et al., 1964a), cannot form specific cell pairs at high frequencies. On the contrary, the formation of[…]","pos":"adj","synonyms":["manly","mannish","masculine","pin"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable, usually","register":"not-comparable, usually","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b0da3bfa6443839e42","definition":"Of instruments, tools, or connectors: designed to fit into or penetrate a female counterpart, as in a connector, pipe fitting or laboratory glassware.","example":"Male adapter connects female pipe threads to polyethylene cold-water pipe; [...] female flare coupling connects male pipe threads to flared copper or plastic;","pos":"adj","synonyms":["plug"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, not-comparable, usually","register":"figuratively, not-comparable, usually","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a50bfeff6c35b1794","definition":"One of the male (masculine) sex or gender.","example":"For quotations using this term, see Citations:male.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["female"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["macho","♂","sex","gender","gender identity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d0e90159c41313c015","definition":"A bacterium which has the F factor.","example":"During mating, F+ male bacteria transfer the F factor to the recipient females, transforming them into F+ males. Males also retain a copy of their F factor for themselves (left). When Hfr (or high frequency recombination) males mate[…]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["female"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["macho","♂","sex","gender","gender identity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:def02f09ae7aaf40f7","definition":"A male connector, pipe fitting, etc.","example":"Work another rubber washer over the threads of the male adapter that is now sticking out of the bucket. […] cut out with an X-acto knife, then thread the female fittings to the males.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["female"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["macho","♂","sex","gender","gender identity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/male#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aa49d7eac4f3ab8e59","definition":"A surname.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["macho","♂","sex","gender","gender identity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Male#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki